INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(231,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/10-largest-global-food-crises-data-and-evidence-worlds-most-severe-food-crises','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/10-largest-global-food-crises-data-and-evidence-worlds-most-severe-food-crises','The 10 Largest Global Food Crises: Data and evidence from the world’s most severe food crises','the10largestglobalfoodcrisesdataandevidencefromtheworldsmostseverefoodcrises','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T07:43:56Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Countries: World, Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Mali, Myanmar, Niger, Nigeria, occupied Palestinian territory, Pakistan, South Sudan, Sudan, Syrian Arab Republic, Yemen Source: Action Against Hunger Please refer to the attached file. NEW YORK, October 15, 2026 – Acute hunger has doubled over the last ten years and now affects 266 million people across 47 countries and territories, according to a new report from Action Against Hunger. Released ahead of World Food Day (October 16), “ The 10 Largest Global Food Crises ” finds that hunger is increasingly concentrated i',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(232,'https://reliefweb.int/report/burundi/burundi-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-le-demarrage-tardif-des-pluies-la-faiblesse-des-revenus-et-la-penurie-dengrais-entravent-le-debut-de-la-saison-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/burundi/burundi-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-le-demarrage-tardif-des-pluies-la-faiblesse-des-revenus-et-la-penurie-dengrais-entravent-le-debut-de-la-saison-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','Burundi - Mise à jour des messages clés : Le démarrage tardif des pluies, la faiblesse des revenus et la pénurie d’engrais entravent le début de la saison A, Septembre 2026 - Janvier 2027','burundimiseajourdesmessagesclesledemarragetardifdespluieslafaiblessedesrevenusetlapenuriedengraisentraventledebutdelasaisonaseptembre2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T02:20:29Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Burundi Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Messages clé La zone de moyens d’existence des Dépressions du Nord devrait passer de résultats de Stress (Phase 2 de l’IPC) à des résultats de Crise (Phase 3 de l’IPC) pendant la période de soudure, entre octobre et janvier. Une partie de la population a déjà épuisé une grande partie de ses capacités d’adaptation après avoir subi des récoltes consécutives inférieures à la moyenne au cours des saisons A et B de 2026. Les ménages ont épuisé leurs stocks alimentaires issus des récoltes de la saison B e',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(233,'https://reliefweb.int/report/cameroon/cameroun-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-les-deficits-pluviometriques-aggravent-les-baisses-de-production-liees-au-conflit-dans-lextreme-nord-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/cameroon/cameroun-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-les-deficits-pluviometriques-aggravent-les-baisses-de-production-liees-au-conflit-dans-lextreme-nord-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','Cameroon: Cameroun - Mise à jour des messages clés : Les déficits pluviométriques aggravent les baisses de production liées au conflit dans l’Extrême-Nord, Septembre 2026 - Janvier 2027','camerooncamerounmiseajourdesmessagescleslesdeficitspluviometriquesaggraventlesbaissesdeproductionlieesauconflitdanslextremenordseptembre2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T02:17:39Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Cameroon Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Messages clé **Dans l’Extrême-Nord, les résultats de Crise (Phase 3 de l’IPC) devraient se poursuivre jusqu’en septembre dans les départements touchés par le conflit tels que Mayo-Sava, Mayo-Tsanaga et Logone-et-Chari, avec certains ménages déplacés très pauvres étant probablement confrontés à d’importants déficits de consommation alimentaire correspondant à l’Urgence (Phase 4 de l’IPC).**Une amélioration vers le Stress (Phase 2 de l’IPC) en octobre est attendue, lorsque les principales récoltes pe',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(234,'https://reliefweb.int/report/madagascar/madagascar-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-soudure-precoce-et-hausse-des-prix-aggravent-linsecurite-alimentaire-dans-le-grand-sud-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/madagascar/madagascar-mise-jour-des-messages-cles-soudure-precoce-et-hausse-des-prix-aggravent-linsecurite-alimentaire-dans-le-grand-sud-septembre-2026-janvier-2027','Madagascar - Mise à jour des messages clés : Soudure précoce et hausse des prix aggravent l’insécurité alimentaire dans le Grand Sud, Septembre 2026 - Janvier 2027','madagascarmiseajourdesmessagesclessoudureprecoceethaussedesprixaggraventlinsecuritealimentairedanslegrandsudseptembre2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T02:14:20Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Madagascar Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Messages clé Les résultats de Crise (Phase 3 de l’IPC) persistent à Toliara II et Amboasary Atsimo et devraient s’étendre à certaines parties du Grand Sud et du Grand Sud-Est à partir d’octobre, à mesure que la période de soudure s’intensifie. Après des récoltes 2025/26 inférieures à la moyenne en raison de pluies irrégulières et de sécheresses prolongées, les ménages pauvres ont épuisé leurs stocks dès septembre, avant le début habituel de la soudure en novembre. Leur dépendance aux marchés augm',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(235,'https://reliefweb.int/report/rwanda/rwanda-flood-simplified-early-action-protocol-activation-eap-no-seap2025rw01-operation-no-mdrrw026-13-october-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/rwanda/rwanda-flood-simplified-early-action-protocol-activation-eap-no-seap2025rw01-operation-no-mdrrw026-13-october-2026','Rwanda | Flood - Simplified Early Action Protocol: Activation (EAP No.: sEAP2025RW01, Operation No.: MDRRW026), 13 October 2026','rwandafloodsimplifiedearlyactionprotocolactivationeapnoseap2025rw01operationnomdrrw02613october2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T01:00:43Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Rwanda Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Please refer to the attached file. EARLY ACTION PROTOCOL ACTIVATION Activation Overview The simplified EAP focuses on the floods in the Rubavu and Nyabihu districts, in the Western Province of Rwanda. The pre-agree triggered if, within the rainy season, Meteo Rwanda’s Dekade forecasts indicate that the next 10-day total rainfall will exceed 90 mm. According to Meteo Rwanda, a forecast dated 10 October predict rainfall amounts ranging between 85 and 105 mm are expected in Rubavu and Musanze Districts, sever',5.0,'classified',NULL,32);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(236,'https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/who-sudan-sudan-health-spotlight-september-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/who-sudan-sudan-health-spotlight-september-2026','WHO Sudan: Sudan Health Spotlight - September 2026','whosudansudanhealthspotlight','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-16T00:07:46Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Sudan Source: World Health Organization Please refer to the attached file. Monthly highlights • Cholera cases continued to decline overall, but transmission remains a concern, with suspected cases still being reported in some localities. Since 15 May 2026, a cumulative 3131 cases and 264 deaths have been reported, corresponding to an overall CFR of 8.0%. • Oral cholera vaccination campaigns achieved high coverage in priority areas. The reactive campaign in Al Fula, An Nuhud and Wad Bandah vaccinated 675 295 people, while second-round campaigns reached 156 983 people in Kas and 83 100 ',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(237,'https://reliefweb.int/report/haiti/haiti-seasonal-monitor-dry-conditions-persist-southern-haiti-october-15-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/haiti/haiti-seasonal-monitor-dry-conditions-persist-southern-haiti-october-15-2026','Haiti - Seasonal Monitor: Dry conditions persist in southern Haiti (October 15, 2026)','haitiseasonalmonitordryconditionspersistinsouthernhaitioctober152026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T19:03:08Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Haiti Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Southern Haiti continues to experience dry conditions. Vegetation conditions continue to deteriorate around Jacmel and Les Cayes, as well as in parts of Ouest and Grand’Anse departments. Below-average rainfall is expected to persist in southern Haiti, negatively affecting normal crop development.',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(238,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-cholera-early-action-framework-getting-ahead-major-cholera-outbreaks-october-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-cholera-early-action-framework-getting-ahead-major-cholera-outbreaks-october-2026','World: Global cholera early action framework: Getting ahead of major cholera outbreaks (As of October 2026)','worldglobalcholeraearlyactionframeworkgettingaheadofmajorcholeraoutbreaksasofoctober2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T17:48:42Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: World Sources: UN Children''s Fund, UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, World Health Organization Please refer to the attached file. 1. Background Cholera remains one of the most devastating yet preventable global public health threats, disproportionately affecting vulnerable populations in fragile settings. The diarrheal disease, which, if untreated, can be fatal, is primarily driven by a lack of access to clean water, proper sanitation and hygiene (WASH), as well as insufficient health services. These are often compounded by conflicts, displacement, climate-relate',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(239,'https://reliefweb.int/report/nepal/too-big-fail-finance-loss-and-damage-rupturing-world','https://reliefweb.int/report/nepal/too-big-fail-finance-loss-and-damage-rupturing-world','Nepal: Too Big to Fail: Finance for Loss and Damage in a Rupturing World','nepaltoobigtofailfinanceforlossanddamageinarupturingworld','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T16:03:08Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Nepal Sources: Caritas, Scottish Catholic International Aid Fund Please refer to the attached file. Caritas calls for radical rethink of climate Loss and Damage finance amid growing geopolitical uncertainty New paper calls for radical rethink of climate Loss and Damage finance amid growing geopolitical uncertainty A new paper from Caritas Internationalis and the Scottish Catholic International Aid Fund (SCIAF) warns that the future of the international Loss and Damage Fund is at risk at precisely the moment when climate impacts are intensifying and global cooperation is under growing ',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(240,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/12th-arab-partnership-disaster-risk-reduction-meeting-commitments-joint-action-open-regional-dialogue-risk-informed-development-and-resilience','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/12th-arab-partnership-disaster-risk-reduction-meeting-commitments-joint-action-open-regional-dialogue-risk-informed-development-and-resilience','World: 12th Arab partnership for disaster risk reduction meeting: From commitments to joint action, an open regional dialogue on risk-informed development and resilience','world12tharabpartnershipfordisasterriskreductionmeetingfromcommitmentstojointactionanopenregionaldialogueonriskinformeddevelopmentandresilience','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T16:03:04Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: World Source: UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction The 12th Arab Partnership for Disaster Risk Reduction Meeting was held in Tunis on 11 October 2026, under the theme “From commitments to joint action: An open regional dialogue on risk-informed development and resilience,” with the participation of representatives from Arab countries, the League of Arab States, United Nations entities, regional organizations, development partners, and Arab stakeholder groups. The meeting aimed to review progress in implementing the Arab Prioritized Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2025–2027, d',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(241,'https://reliefweb.int/report/yemen/cholera-outbreak-spreading-rapidly-yemen-more-people-flee-violence','https://reliefweb.int/report/yemen/cholera-outbreak-spreading-rapidly-yemen-more-people-flee-violence','Cholera outbreak spreading rapidly in Yemen as more people flee violence','choleraoutbreakspreadingrapidlyinyemenasmorepeoplefleeviolence','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T12:49:39Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Yemen Source: Islamic Relief Cholera cases have tripled in the last three weeks in southern Yemen as the conflict and displacement escalates, and Islamic Relief is warning that thousands of lives are at risk. The fighting has caused over 200,000 people to seek refuge in overcrowded and polluted camps and other sites such as mosques and schools. About 40% of the displaced people do not have access to safe water and one third don’t have proper latrines, forcing families to defecate outside – conditions that are breeding grounds for the spread of fatal water-borne diseases such as choler',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(242,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/commissioners-kubilius-and-lahbib-strengthen-global-disaster-risk-management-through-space-technologies-0','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/commissioners-kubilius-and-lahbib-strengthen-global-disaster-risk-management-through-space-technologies-0','World: Commissioners Kubilius and Lahbib strengthen global disaster risk management through space technologies','worldcommissionerskubiliusandlahbibstrengthenglobaldisasterriskmanagementthroughspacetechnologies','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T01:50:43Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: World Source: European Commission Please refer to the attached files. On the occasion of the International Day for Disaster Risk Management, the European Commission is convening the very first cross-regional dialogue ‘From Space to Grassroots: Strengthening Community Resilience to Natural Hazards through Space Technologies''. The dialogue marked the start of a process to further strengthen international cooperation to anticipate, prepare for and respond to disasters using space technologies. The dialogue identified opportunities for closer cooperation with partners worldwide, from impr',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(243,'https://reliefweb.int/report/guatemala/guatemala-key-message-update-delays-and-damage-staple-grain-harvests-prolong-lean-season-september-2026-january-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/guatemala/guatemala-key-message-update-delays-and-damage-staple-grain-harvests-prolong-lean-season-september-2026-january-2027','Guatemala - Key Message Update: Delays and damage to staple grain harvests prolong the lean season, September 2026 - January 2027','guatemalakeymessageupdatedelaysanddamagetostaplegrainharvestsprolongtheleanseasonseptember2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T01:33:52Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Guatemala Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages In September, areas of the Dry Corridor, Alta Verapaz, and Western Highlands are classified in Crisis (IPC Phase 3) , where very poor subsistence farming households account for a large proportion of the population and have experienced the most severe staple grain crop losses. Harvest delays and damage, coupled with reduced agricultural wages earned during the staple grain planting and maintenance season, have reduced both household food stocks from own production and available income.',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(244,'https://reliefweb.int/report/guatemala/guatemala-actualizacion-de-mensajes-clave-retrasos-y-danos-en-cosechas-de-granos-basicos-prolongan-temporada-de-escasez-septiembre-2026-enero-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/guatemala/guatemala-actualizacion-de-mensajes-clave-retrasos-y-danos-en-cosechas-de-granos-basicos-prolongan-temporada-de-escasez-septiembre-2026-enero-2027','Guatemala - Actualización de mensajes clave: Retrasos y daños en cosechas de granos básicos prolongan temporada de escasez, Septiembre 2026 - Enero 2027','guatemalaactualizaciondemensajesclaveretrasosydanosencosechasdegranosbasicosprolongantemporadadeescasezseptiembre2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T01:33:48Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Guatemala Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Mensajes Clave En septiembre, áreas del Corredor Seco, Alta Verapaz y Altiplano Occidental se clasifican en Crisis (Fase 3, CIF) ,donde los hogares de agricultores de subsistencia muy pobres constituyen una gran parte de la población y experimentaron las pérdidas más severas de cultivos de granos básicos. Los retrasos y daños a las cosechas, junto con la reducción de jornales percibidos durante la temporada de siembra y mantenimiento de granos básicos, disminuyeron tanto las reservas de alimentos ',5.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(245,'https://reliefweb.int/report/venezuela-bolivarian-republic/venezuela-key-message-update-limited-purchasing-power-despite-gradual-macroeconomic-and-earthquake-recovery-september-2026-january-2027','https://reliefweb.int/report/venezuela-bolivarian-republic/venezuela-key-message-update-limited-purchasing-power-despite-gradual-macroeconomic-and-earthquake-recovery-september-2026-january-2027','Venezuela - Key Message Update: Limited purchasing power despite gradual macroeconomic and earthquake recovery, September 2026 - January 2027','venezuelakeymessageupdatelimitedpurchasingpowerdespitegradualmacroeconomicandearthquakerecoveryseptember2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T01:24:16Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of) Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Key Messages Poor households negatively affected by the June 24 earthquakes continue to face Crisis (IPC Phase 3) outcomes, particularly in Distrito Capital (Caracas) and Aragua, where housing losses, damage to productive assets, and limited income-earning opportunities continue to slow recovery. Humanitarian food assistance is supporting food access and preventing wider food consumption gaps in La Guaira, resulting in Stressed! (IPC Phase 2!) outcomes. In Yaracuy and Cara',6.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(246,'https://reliefweb.int/report/kenya/early-warning-information-ecosystem-mapping-turkana-west-county-kenya-november-december-2025','https://reliefweb.int/report/kenya/early-warning-information-ecosystem-mapping-turkana-west-county-kenya-november-december-2025','Early Warning Information Ecosystem Mapping Turkana West County, Kenya (November - December 2025)','earlywarninginformationecosystemmappingturkanawestcountykenyanovember','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-15T00:00:00Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Kenya Source: Welthungerhilfe Everyone in society needs, and has a right to, the best possible forecast information so they can make the best informed decisions for themselves as individuals, families, communities, businesses or governments . Every year hundreds of millions of people globally are affected by protracted hunger, conflict and perennial weather-related risks, creating an increasingly greater need for humanitarian action. The climate crisis exacerbates and compounds these shocks and their impacts on people. Changing weather patterns, including unusually heavy rainfall, can',4.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(247,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-weather-hazards-summary-october-15-2026-october-21-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/global-weather-hazards-summary-october-15-2026-october-21-2026','World: Global Weather Hazards Summary, October 15, 2026 – October 21, 2026','worldglobalweatherhazardssummaryoctober152026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-14T20:03:09Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: World Source: Famine Early Warning System Network Please refer to the attached file. Global Overview : El Niño continues to strengthen. Long-term abnormal dryness and abnormal heat persist across areas of Africa, northern Central Asia, Central America, Hispaniola, and northern South America. Africa Weather Hazards Abnormal heat is forecast in the eastern Sahel and parts of Eastern Africa, while high risks of flooding with ongoing heavy rain in the horn of Africa. 1) Inundation in the Sudd wetlands of South Sudan persists. 2) Large 90-day rainfall deficits have led to abnormal dryness ',8.0,'classified',NULL,14);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(248,'https://reliefweb.int/report/djibouti/djibouti-seap-flood-simplified-early-action-protocol-activation-mdrdj009-12102026','https://reliefweb.int/report/djibouti/djibouti-seap-flood-simplified-early-action-protocol-activation-mdrdj009-12102026','Djibouti | sEAP Flood - Simplified Early Action Protocol: Activation (MDRDJ009), 12/10/2026','djiboutiseapfloodsimplifiedearlyactionprotocolactivationmdrdj00912102026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-14T13:47:43Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Djibouti Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Please refer to the attached file. Activation Overview Djibouti Red Crescent National Society has activated it’s Simplified Early Action Protocol for Flood. Djibouti seasonal forecast for October-December shows a rainfall impact related to the El Nino event. In line with this outlook ICPAC has released a weekly forecast that indicates a potential rainfall in the coastal zones including Djibouti, Tadjourah, obock, Arta and few areas of Ali Sabieh will be affected. National Society has been monitoring the ',4.0,'classified',NULL,4);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(249,'https://reliefweb.int/report/chad/tcd-food-insecurity-10-2026-food-crisis-due-rainfall-deficit','https://reliefweb.int/report/chad/tcd-food-insecurity-10-2026-food-crisis-due-rainfall-deficit','Chad: TCD: Food Insecurity - 10-2026 - Food crisis due to rainfall deficit','chadtcdfoodinsecurity102026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-14T13:44:47Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Country: Chad Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Sources for data marked as Other Estimates of the 2,990,000 people potentially affected by food insecurity are based on FEWS NET analyses. The figure of 294,800 displaced people is taken from data published by the Food Security Cluster on July 29, 2026. Description The 2026 agropastoral season in Chad is marked by a significant rainfall deficit, a late and irregular onset of the rainy season and an unusual extension of the lean season. In several regions of the country, rainfall remained below the seasonal a',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(250,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/wfp-eastern-and-southern-africa-seasonal-outlook-eastern-and-southern-africa-regional-office-esaro-october-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/wfp-eastern-and-southern-africa-seasonal-outlook-eastern-and-southern-africa-regional-office-esaro-october-2026','World: WFP Eastern and Southern Africa Seasonal Outlook: Eastern and Southern Africa Regional Office (ESARO) - October 2026','worldwfpeasternandsouthernafricaseasonaloutlookeasternandsouthernafricaregionalofficeesaro','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-14T12:21:46Z','2026-10-16T15:26:20Z','Countries: World, Angola, Burundi, Congo, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Djibouti, Eswatini, Ethiopia, Kenya, Lesotho, Madagascar, Malawi, Rwanda, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Uganda, United Republic of Tanzania, Zambia, Zimbabwe Source: World Health Organization Please refer to the attached file. Highlights • Above-normal rainfall and above-average temperatures are favoured across much of Eastern Africa during October to December 2026. Southern Ethiopia, central and southern Somalia and Kenya show the strongest wet signal, increasing extreme rainfall and flood risks. • Much of central and ',1.0,'classified',NULL,3);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(251,'https://reliefweb.int/report/chile/chl-erupcion-volcanica-07-2026-actualizacion-erupcion-volcanica-2-2026-10-14','https://reliefweb.int/report/chile/chl-erupcion-volcanica-07-2026-actualizacion-erupcion-volcanica-2-2026-10-14','Chile: CHL: Erupción volcánica - 07-2026 - Actualización Erupción Volcánica #2 (2026-10-14)','chilechlerupcionvolcanica072026actualizacionerupcionvolcanica220261014','reliefweb_ew_es','ReliefWeb - Updates','es','2026-10-15T00:37:30Z','2026-10-16T15:26:22Z','Country: Chile Sources: Cruz Roja Chilena, International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies Please refer to the attached file. Descripción De acuerdo con la información proporcionada por el Observatorio Volcánico de los Andes del Sur (OVDAS) del Servicio Nacional de Geología y Minería (SERNAGEOMIN), el Complejo Volcánico Nevados de Chillán mantiene la alerta técnica en nivel Amarillo. En relación con el Reporte Especial de Actividad Volcánica (REAV) emitido hoy miércoles 14 de octubre, las estaciones de monitoreo instaladas en las inmediaciones del complejo volcánico Nevados de',2.0,'classified',NULL,15);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(252,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/sensitivity-observed-changes-compound-climate-extremes','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/sensitivity-observed-changes-compound-climate-extremes','Sensitivity of observed changes in compound climate extremes across Europe to event definition','sensitivityofobservedchangesincompoundclimateextremesacrosseuropetoeventdefinition','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-16T10:31:23Z','2026-10-16T15:26:23Z','This article assesses how definitions affect detected changes in compound climate extremes in Europe, finding that event frequency, intensity, and trends are sensitive to metric choice and recommends careful selection of event definitions for monitoring.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(253,'https://www.preventionweb.net/news/disasters-cost-228-billion-housing-losses-every-year','https://preventionweb.net/news/disasters-cost-228-billion-housing-losses-every-year','Disasters cost $228 billion in housing losses every year','disasterscost228billioninhousinglosseseveryyear','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-16T10:09:39Z','2026-10-16T15:26:23Z','Marking the International Day for Disaster Risk Reduction, the UN chief stressed that “as climate and disaster risks multiply, building safer dwellings is the shared responsibility of governments, developers, engineers and communities”.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(254,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/diagnosing-region-specific-flood-influencing-factors','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/diagnosing-region-specific-flood-influencing-factors','Diagnosing region-specific flood influencing factors in a volcanic island using explainable machine learning','diagnosingregionspecificfloodinfluencingfactorsinavolcanicislandusingexplainablemachinelearning','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-16T09:56:00Z','2026-10-16T15:26:23Z','This study applies a grid-based, explainable machine learning framework to Jeju Island and finds that rainfall, groundwater, and proximity to water bodies are key, regionally variable factors for flood occurrence, supporting nuanced flood risk management.',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(255,'https://www.preventionweb.net/drr-community-voices/rethinking-disaster-reconstruction-nepal-building-back-changing-climate','https://preventionweb.net/drr-community-voices/rethinking-disaster-reconstruction-nepal-building-back-changing-climate','Rethinking disaster reconstruction in Nepal: Building back for a changing climate','rethinkingdisasterreconstructioninnepalbuildingbackforachangingclimate','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-16T09:15:21Z','2026-10-16T15:26:23Z','Repeated floods in Nepal’s mountain and hill regions made the author raise a fundamental question: should reconstruction simply restore what was lost, or should it address the changing risks that made those communities vulnerable in the first place?',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
