INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2105,'https://reliefweb.int/report/syrian-arab-republic/strengthening-syrias-disaster-preparedness-and-response-through-early-warning-and-anticipatory-action','https://reliefweb.int/report/syrian-arab-republic/strengthening-syrias-disaster-preparedness-and-response-through-early-warning-and-anticipatory-action','Strengthening Syria’s Disaster Preparedness and Response through Early Warning and Anticipatory Action','strengtheningsyriasdisasterpreparednessandresponsethroughearlywarningandanticipatoryaction','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-20T02:26:37Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Country: Syrian Arab Republic Source: Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations The Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO), together with the Ministry of Emergency and Disaster Management (MoEDM) and consortium partners: the International Organization for Migration (IOM), the United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR), Mercy Corps, the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), the Danish Refugee Council (DRC), officially launched a new project funded by the European Civil Protection and Humanitarian Aid Operations (ECHO), which focuses on strengthenin',6.0,'classified',NULL,87);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2106,'https://reliefweb.int/report/somalia/anticipatory-action-implementation-plan-somalia-floods','https://reliefweb.int/report/somalia/anticipatory-action-implementation-plan-somalia-floods','Anticipatory Action Implementation Plan Somalia - Floods','anticipatoryactionimplementationplansomalia','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-19T19:21:08Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Country: Somalia Source: UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs Please refer to the attached file. Executive Summary The humanitarian community is increasingly scaling up Anticipatory Action (AA) to enable proactive responses to predictable climate-related shocks. By combining robust forecasting systems, pre-agreed activities, and pre-arranged financing, anticipatory action enables humanitarian actors to act before disasters occur, reducing human suffering, protecting livelihoods, preserving development gains, and delivering assistance in a more dignified, timely, and cost-effe',3.0,'classified',NULL,35);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2107,'https://reliefweb.int/report/uganda/resilience-starts-home-preparing-communities-el-nino-disaster-strikes','https://reliefweb.int/report/uganda/resilience-starts-home-preparing-communities-el-nino-disaster-strikes','Uganda: Resilience starts at home: Preparing communities for El Niño before disaster strikes','ugandaresiliencestartsathomepreparingcommunitiesforelninobeforedisasterstrikes','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-19T08:33:13Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Countries: Uganda, Kenya Source: International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies In parts of the Karamoja region, north-eastern Uganda, the effects of prolonged drought are already visible. Water sources have dried up or fallen to very low levels. Families are travelling further to find water, while pasture continues to deteriorate, putting pressure on livelihoods that depend on livestock and crop production. One of the clearest signs of the worsening situation is Kobebe Dam in Karamoja’s Moroto district, normally a critical source of water for communities and their livestock.',1.0,'classified',NULL,77);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2108,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/disaster-risk-reduction-2025-key-achievements','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/disaster-risk-reduction-2025-key-achievements','World: Disaster Risk Reduction: 2025 Key Achievements','worlddisasterriskreduction2025keyachievements','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-19T07:35:03Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Countries: World, Pakistan, Somalia, South Sudan Source: International Organization for Migration Please refer to the attached file. In 2025, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) continued to support governments, communities, migrants and displaced populations to better anticipate, withstand and recover from disasters and climate-related hazards. Through community-based preparedness, early warning systems, risk-informed planning, anticipatory action and mobilitysensitive approaches to recovery and resilience, IOM advanced the Sendai Framework and worked to prevent and reduce disp',6.0,'classified',NULL,76);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2109,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/joint-solidarity-remarks-joining-forces-alliance-48th-ordinary-session-african-committee-experts-rights-and-welfare-child-acerwc-15-oct-2026','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/joint-solidarity-remarks-joining-forces-alliance-48th-ordinary-session-african-committee-experts-rights-and-welfare-child-acerwc-15-oct-2026','World: Joint Solidarity remarks by Joining Forces Alliance: 48th Ordinary Session of the African Committee of Experts on the Rights and Welfare of the Child (ACERWC) (15 Oct 2026)','worldjointsolidarityremarksbyjoiningforcesalliance48thordinarysessionoftheafricancommitteeofexpertsontherightsandwelfareofthechildacerwc15oct2026','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-19T04:20:49Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Country: World Sources: ChildFund Alliance, Plan International, Save the Children, SOS Children''s Villages International, Terre des hommes, World Vision Please refer to the attached file. Honorable Chairperson of the African Committee of Experts on the Rights and Welfare of the Child, Esteemed Committee Members, Distinguished Representatives of Member States, Children of Africa, Ladies and Gentlemen, all protocols observed. We, the Joining Forces Alliance namely: Child Fund Alliance, Plan International, Save the Children International, SOS Children’s Villages International, Terre des Hommes In',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2110,'https://reliefweb.int/report/world/disasters-cost-228-billion-housing-losses-every-year','https://reliefweb.int/report/world/disasters-cost-228-billion-housing-losses-every-year','World: Disasters cost $228 billion in housing losses every year','worlddisasterscost228billioninhousinglosseseveryyear','reliefweb_ew_en','ReliefWeb - Updates','en','2026-10-17T08:33:04Z','2026-10-20T03:07:51Z','Countries: World, Colombia, Nepal, Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of) Source: UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction $228 billion is a staggering amount of money to find, but that’s exactly what communities around the world are faced with every year, to rebuild housing after disaster strikes. Highlighting the need for greater investment in stronger homes and better preparedness, UN Secretary-General António Guterres said that millions of homes are damaged or destroyed annually “displacing families and deepening poverty”. Marking the International Day for Disaster Risk Reduction , the UN chief s',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2111,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/rethinking-potential-flood-damage-assessment-data-driven','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/rethinking-potential-flood-damage-assessment-data-driven','Rethinking potential flood damage assessment: a data-driven alternative to Varnes-based models','rethinkingpotentialflooddamageassessmentadatadrivenalternativetovarnesbasedmodels','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-19T15:04:49Z','2026-10-20T03:07:52Z','The authors present an innovative, data-driven methodology for mapping susceptibility to flood damage to private assets, leveraging machine learning techniques to overcome some of the limitations and uncertainties associated with traditional approaches.',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2112,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/risk-knowledge-action-systematic-review-and-evidence-map','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/risk-knowledge-action-systematic-review-and-evidence-map','From risk knowledge to action: A systematic review and evidence map of institutionalization deficits in non-structural urban flood risk reduction','fromriskknowledgetoactionasystematicreviewandevidencemapofinstitutionalizationdeficitsinnonstructuralurbanfloodriskreduction','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-19T15:01:42Z','2026-10-20T03:07:52Z','This study applies an a priori scaffold of eight institutionalisation pathways and a cross-cutting coordination pathway to develop an institutionalisation-deficit framework.',1.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2113,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/bridging-gap-between-damaged-infrastructures-and-disaster','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/bridging-gap-between-damaged-infrastructures-and-disaster','Bridging the gap between damaged infrastructures and disaster mortality','bridgingthegapbetweendamagedinfrastructuresanddisastermortality','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-19T14:52:58Z','2026-10-20T03:07:52Z','This study analysed the relationship between infrastructure damage and disaster impact. It does so by scraping 79 Post Disaster Needs Assessment reports to collect disaster specific infrastructure damage data for 79 disaster events of this century.',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(2114,'https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/geoglam-crop-monitor-early-warning-report-october-2026','https://preventionweb.net/publication/documents-and-publications/geoglam-crop-monitor-early-warning-report-october-2026','GEOGLAM Crop Monitor for Early Warning report: October 2026','geoglamcropmonitorforearlywarningreportoctober2026','preventionweb','PreventionWeb','en','2026-10-19T14:40:26Z','2026-10-20T03:07:52Z','The October 2026 GEOGLAM Crop Monitor for Early Warning report provides an overview of global crop conditions with a focus on regions vulnerable to food insecurity.',3.0,'classified',NULL,NULL);
